{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7723","id":5212013510,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNqkDxg","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7723","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7723.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7723.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7723","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7723/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7723/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7723/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/fc1c796be37d5018294f6a867a18daa7dead348e","number":7723,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"github-backup: mirror contract remainder (#3238, #3270, #3240, #3283)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #3238, closes #3270, closes #3240, closes #3283 — the four open children of design #3282 (\"a mirror is what it can prove\"), driven by queue task 12622. The other phase children (#3233, #3250, #3219, #3257, #3229) are already closed, so this PR completes the design's acceptance: no surface of the system can report coverage, success, or health the underlying mirrors, records, or inventory do not support.\n\n## #3238 — validity is resolvability (design rule 1–2)\n- `ghb_common.valid_mirror` now requires bareness AND a resolvable HEAD (`rev-parse --verify -q HEAD`). No emptiness exception: planned repos are never legitimately empty (build_plan excludes zero-commit repos), documented in the docstring.\n- New `ghb_common.is_skeleton_mirror` (bare + unresolvable HEAD + zero refs); `clone_all.dest_is_confirmed_partial` treats a skeleton as a confirmed partial, so a killed clone's skeleton is cleared and re-cloned instead of being preserved forever by the #3233 policy guard. A bare repo WITH refs is still preserved.\n\n## #3270 — a missing mirror reaches the alarm (design rule 5)\n- `fetch_mirrors.fetch_repo` records a missing mirror as an unavailable day through the same `fail_days` streak as failures (#3257 semantics): 3 consecutive missing days now make the daily run exit 1. Success clears the record via the existing reset. The drainer shares the recorder, and same-day repeats count once.\n\n## #3240 — state written atomically, loaded tolerantly, only through ghb_common (design rule 6)\n- New helpers in `ghb_common`: `atomic_write_text` (temp file in the same directory + fsync + `os.replace` + last-good copy), `save_json`, `load_json_tolerant` (torn file → last-good copy, else empty, always with a loud named problem), and `state_lock` (shared flock).\n- `load_plan` / `load_state` route through the tolerant loader — a torn plan.json/state.json no longer wedges fetch, drainer, clone pass, manifest, or reconcile at startup.\n- All generated-state writers migrated: fetch + drain state.json saves, reconcile plan.json, manifest MANIFEST.json, FAMILIES.md, and the dated reconcile report. Both state.json writers hold `state_lock` across their whole load→modify→save cycle, closing the lost-update window.\n\n## #3283 — closing audit\n- The grep inventory of remaining bare `json.load` / `open(\"w\")` / file `json.dump` in `infra/github-backup/bin/` is posted on #3283 with a disposition for every hit: after this PR the only file-IO hits are the ghb_common helpers themselves, `load_config` (repo source file, not generated state), subprocess/API payload parsing, and append-only logs (out of the torn-write class by the audit's own scope).\n- Named dispositions: (a) FAMILIES.md + reconcile report — migrated to the atomic helper in this PR; (b) drainer plan load — already a single pre-loop load, now through the tolerant loader; (c) Worker (`worker/src/index.js`) — out of scope, KV is its store (recorded on #3283).\n- Contract statement: the seven rules in operator language are now in `infra/github-backup/README.md`, cross-referenced from the DR section of `docs/RUNBOOK.md`. Completion evidence is posted on umbrella #3215.\n\n## Tests\n- New `tests/test_mirror_contract.py`: skeleton invalid + complete mirror valid (real git repos), skeleton confirmed-partial vs complete preserved, manifest reports a skeleton `missing`, missing-day streak accumulation + chronic exit 1 through `main()` + clear-on-ok, atomic roundtrip/last-good fallback/torn-without-backup/intact-on-failed-replace, state lock.\n- One existing expectation updated: `test_plan_state_shape.py::test_main_survives_state_top_level_list` — the saved state now also carries the #3270 missing-day record for the (patched-invalid) repo; the #6637 wrong-shape contract it guards is unchanged.\n- Three existing fixture helpers updated (`test_clone_all_partial.py`, `test_reconcile_clone_pass.py`, `test_reconcile_retention.py`): their \"valid mirror\" fixtures were `git init --bare` skeletons — the exact shape #3238 makes invalid — so they now seed one real commit. The behaviours those suites guard (#3233 partial clearance, #3300 clone-pass propagation, #3229 retention) are unchanged.\n- Full github-backup suite run on the laptop before merge; all suites pass.\n\n🤖 Queue worker lane code-g, task 12622.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796739138&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7723&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7723&signature=2e57efea178cc22f6c86e0afe1fc5595a3f9c76cad93dce2ae0ec5c64538a14c\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7723?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T14:12:14Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T15:04:07Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T15:04:05Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T15:04:05Z","merge_commit_sha":"752357c139ba7cec16cdedf658236ebf17df4ae6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"